TALLY_FINAL_MESSAGE={"verdict":"transient","diagnosis":"Aborted in the lane stage before any worktree was prepared, so no worker ever ran and no task content was implicated. The recorded failure is a flow-error whose detail is the harness exception FlowAdmissionDenied (code admission-denied, ordinal 4, at line 3377 column 25) with an empty details object; exitCode is null and captureStderr is empty, meaning no command was executed and no gate ran. gateOutputs is empty, workerOutcomeClaim is null, previousWorkerOutcomes and previousDiagnoses are empty, and the diff is unavailable with reason 'task failed before a worktree was prepared' at base rev all-zeros. Nothing in the task morning-ledger points at the failure: the sole acceptance criterion ledger-sections is a plain grep over docs/MORNING.md and docs/ANNOUNCE.md, both inside the authorized docs conflict domain, and it was never evaluated. The dependencies host-tooling and bench-harness are also not implicated, because dependency resolution would surface as a task-level block rather than an admission denial raised inside the flow engine itself. Admission denial at lane entry with no stderr, no exit code, and no worktree is a scheduler/session fault in the machinery that admits lanes, not an authorable defect in the repository and not a gate-contract or authority problem the operator must grant. The correct disposition is therefore to charge the bounded machinery-retry budget and re-admit the lane unchanged; if admission is denied again at the same ordinal, the fault is durable in the flow layer and should be escalated to the operator rather than retried further."}
